WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.045
NIST Special Publication 800-53 is a catalog of security and privacy controls used to help

00:00:06.045 --> 00:00:07.870
organizations manage cybersecurity risk.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.961
Developed by the National Institute of Standards and Technology,

00:00:10.961 --> 00:00:15.310
it provides guidance for selecting and implementing safeguards that protect information

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:16.520
systems and data.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.922
Although originally created for federal systems,

00:00:18.922 --> 00:00:22.720
NIST SP 800-53 has influenced security programs across government,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.280
critical infrastructure, healthcare, education, finance, and commercial industries.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.180
The key idea is that organizations need a structured way to define safeguards,

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.710
assign responsibility, assess effectiveness, and improve security and privacy over time.
